.TH EMAIL\-SYNC 1 "" "email-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
email\-sync \- background mail synchroniser for email-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B email\-sync
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B email\-sync cron
.RB { setup | status | remove }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B email\-sync
downloads new mail into the local store so that
.BR email\-cli (1),
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1)
and
.BR email\-tui (1)
can read \- and search \- without contacting the server.
.PP
Run it before searching: the content search only sees messages that are
already cached.
.PP
Gmail accounts use the History API for incremental runs and fall back to a
full reconcile when the stored history ID has expired. IMAP accounts use
CONDSTORE/QRESYNC when the server offers it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-account " email"
Sync only this account instead of all of them.
.TP
.B \-\-reconcile
Force a full listing instead of the incremental path.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild\-index
Rebuild label index files from cached headers. Offline; fixes zero or wrong
counts without re\-downloading.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild\-contacts
Rebuild the contact suggestion cache from cached headers. Offline.
.TP
.B \-\-apply\-rules
Apply the account's sorting rules to already\-cached messages, then push the
resulting flag changes to the server.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Report each rule that fires and each message that changes.
.TP
.B \-\-help ", " \-h
Show help.
.SH CRON
.TP
.B cron setup
Install a crontab entry that runs a sync every
.I SYNC_INTERVAL
minutes.
.TP
.B cron status
Report whether the entry is installed.
.TP
.B cron remove
Remove the entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/email\-cli/logs/sync-session.log
Sync diagnostics.
.PP
Store and configuration paths are as in
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non\-zero on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR email\-cli (1),
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1),
.BR email\-tui (1)
